{
 "_about": "A pumped two-zone default room as Jev 3.11.1 left it, recorded by running that release's own wizard and controller (v3.11.1, 12c6d1a) in a real Home Assistant 2026.9.3 with every Jev answer stubbed and no network, not written by hand. Pump + main line + two valves with the declared plumbing 'pump_mainline_valves', two probes on zone 1, a uS/cm EC probe on zone 2, feed EC/pH mapped, lights 6-18, a batch-tank doser in 'states' (its dosing setup is dosing_3_11_1.json). The operator set the four ladder numbers of each zone and zone 2's plant count, and turned Auto setpoints on; the room then ran two grow-days under 3.11.1's controller, which moved each zone's ladder to the zone's highest readings and its learner moved the re-water threshold. 'operator_tuned_numbers' are those numbers as Home Assistant then held them, with the attributes 3.11.1 stored beside them; 'moved_by_the_controller' are the ones the controller wrote, with the value it wrote. 'registry' is every entity id 3.11.1 registered for this entry, keyed to its unique-id suffix. The app's options are options_3_11_1_jev_cf.json, its /data/state.json state_3_11_1_learn_jev.json and its /data/jev_usage.json jev_usage_3_11_1.json.",
